  "details": "so I currently use a PSVR2 on VRChat and I don't really have the best PC I have a RTX 3050 and a i5 10400F, But I have noticed I can run other games smoothly and there is only one difference and its a app where it, I'm guessing \"detects\" using the IR Cameras where I'm looking and ONLY makes that the actual resolution  and everywhere else outside of my main vision (so like where your actual focus is) is like lower quality and this makes MANY games runnable and actually get HIGH FPS. I'd like to see this added as it would be useful especially for people who don't have all that good of a PC. This app I use currently doesn't work with VRChat because of EAC so I'd like to see VRChat implement something like this",
